    "edit": {
        "tabs": {
            "quickStart": {
                "heading": "Add Daon TrustX",
                "subHeading": "Follow the steps below to add Daon TrustX verification and login to your application.",
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "title": "Configure the connection",
                        "content": "<p>Provide the <strong>Client ID</strong>, <strong>Client Secret</strong>, <strong>endpoint URLs</strong>, <strong>Scopes</strong>, and the <strong>Login</strong> and <strong>Enrol</strong> process definitions on the <strong>Settings</strong> tab, and register the authorized redirect URI shown there as an allowed redirect URI of the OIDC client in your Daon TrustX tenant.</p>"
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Map attributes",
                        "content": "<p>On the <strong>Attributes</strong> tab, map Daon verified claims (e.g. <Code class=\"inline-code\">given_name</Code>, <Code class=\"inline-code\">family_name</Code>, <Code class=\"inline-code\">birthdate</Code>) to WSO2 local claims. These drive provisioning and verification.</p>"
                    },
                    {
                        "title": "Add Daon TrustX to a flow",
                        "content": "<p>Add <strong>Daon TrustX</strong> to a registration flow (to verify and provision new users) or to an application's <strong>Login Flow</strong> as a step after the user is identified (to verify or enrol at login).</p>"
                    }
                ]
            },
